    <l n="1" para="true">Formam dicunt Peripatetici; ac proinde</l>
    <l n="2">perperam ab ijs Materiæ nomine censentur,</l>
    <l n="3">1, III, 30. &amp; §. 33, p. Corpus ab Anima</l>
    <l n="4">habet vitam, non ut sit unum &amp;</l>
    <l n="5">hoc aliquid, 102, f. 103, p. Corpus naturale esse Physicæ</l>
    <l n="6">subjectum, à Peripateticis rectè dicitur,</l>
    <l n="7">si sano modo intelligatur, 1, I, 1. Corporum</l>
    <l n="8">duntaxat Principia Aristoteles &amp; Prisci tra-</l>
    <l n="9">diderunt, incorporeis neglectis, 2, III, 10.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="2" para="true">A corporis humani structurâ, ordienda</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="2">Medicina, 1, I, 2.</l>
    <l n="12">Corpus naturale nullum est acervus, 327,</l>
    <l n="13">p. Corporum organicorum figura, 264, m.</l>
    <l n="14">CORRUPTIO. vi. INTERITUS.</l>
    <l n="15">CRASIS. vi. TEMPERAMENTUM.</l>
    <l n="16" type="heading" level="2" para="true">CREATIO.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Peripateticum dogma, Creationem non</l>
    <l n="18">esse nisi rerum per se subsistentium, 1, III,</l>
    <l n="19">47, p. absurditatis coarguitur, §. 2.</l>
    <l n="20">Deus post primam Mundi septimanam, nullam</l>
    <l n="21">Substantiam creat ex nihilo, 144, m. Creari</l>
    <l n="22">Formas, dixit Avicenna cum aliis nonnul-</l>
    <l n="23">lis; quibus reliqui Peripatetici magnopere</l>
    <l n="24">exclamant, 1 III, 48. A ratione abhorret,</l>
    <l n="25">prorsi Generationi adjungere creationem,</l>
    <l n="26">247, p. Substantias ex nihilo creandi</l>
    <l n="27">potentiam Deo adimunt Aristoteles cæterique</l>
    <l n="28">Philosophi, 182, p. vi. NIHILUM.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">CURIOSITAS non ita fugienda, ut in</l>
    <l n="30">contrarium vitium incidamus, &amp; pro æqua-</l>
    <l n="31">nimis stolidi inveniamur, 114, p.</l>
