    <l n="41" para="true">DELIBERARE, vi. Βουλεύεσθαι.</l>
    <l n="42" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DEMOCRITUS.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">Democriti opinio de Forma, passim Ari-</l>
    <l n="44">stoteli usurpata, quanquam ab eo damnata,</l>
    <l n="45">3, III, 4, &amp; 5. Democriti sententia de Mundi</l>
    <l n="46">ortu, 315, m. Democriti &amp; Leucippi opinio</l>
    <l n="47">de primarijs Materiæ affectionibus, 331, p.</l>
    <l n="48" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DENSITAS, vi. RARITAS.</l>
    <l n="49" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DEUS.</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">* Præter Deum omnes Substantiæ sunt</l>
    <l n="51">corpora, physicè compositæ, 1, I, 1. Deum</l>
    <l n="52">Mundi opificem agnoverunt prisci Physio-</l>
    <l n="53">logi ante Aristotelem omnes, 314, f. &amp; seqq.</l>
    <l n="54">Deo potentiam, substantias ex nihilo crean-</l>
    <l n="55">di, adēmit Aristoteles cum cæteris Philoso-</l>
    <l n="56">phis, 182, p. Deus <i>arctissimum</i> quendam</l>
    <l n="57">inter Animæ facultates consensū ordinavit,</l>
    <l n="58">84, f. * <i>Divina institutio</i>, unica causa,</l>
    <l n="59">unde specifice differentiæ dependent, 1, III, 20.</l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DIFFERENTIA.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">Ad Specificas rerum Differentias consti-</l>
    <l n="62">tuendas, sola Materia cum Accidentibus</l>
    <l n="63">sufficit, 1, III, 9. * Differentiæ specificæ in</l>
    <l n="64">primaria Dei institutione habent suum</l>
    <l n="65">fundamentum, 1, III, 20. Differentia rerum</l>
    <l n="66">Essentialis non tollitur, sublatâ Formâ,</l>
    <l n="67">quod metuunt Peripatetici, p. 48.</l>
    <l n="68" para="true">DISSENTIRE à Prisicis sæpe quæsivit</l>
    <l n="69">Aristoteles, etiam ubi plane ipsorum seque-</l>
    <l n="70">batur opinionem, 320, f.</l>
    <l n="71" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DISSIMILARIA.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">Partes Dissimilares perperam Integrant-</l>
    <l n="73">ibus annumerantur in Periparo, 267, f. Dis-</l>
    <l n="74">similares Partes duorum generum, Essent-</l>
    <l n="75">iales, &amp; Conformantes, 2, II, 16. Partium</l>
    <l n="76">Dissimilarium characterismus, 6. 18.</l>
    <l n="77" para="true">DISTINCTIO frigida inter inhærentem Formæ &amp;</l>
    <l n="78">Accidentium, 1, III, 35. nulla tanta difficultas, è qua non alicujus Distin-</l>
    <l n="79">ctiunculæ ope se expediant Aristotelici,</l>
    <l n="80">160, p.</l>
    <l n="81" para="true">DIVINUM Causæ genus quid Platoni, 2, V, 5.</l>
    <l n="82" para="true">DIVINA Institutio, vi. DEUS.</l>
    <l n="83" type="heading" level="2" para="true">DIVISIO.</l>
    <l n="84" para="true">Divisio</l>
    <l n="85">nihil est aliud quam Partium</l>
    <l n="86">sejunctio: ideoq; quicquid verè dividitur,</l>
    <l n="87">necessariò est è Partibus concretum,</l>
    <l n="88">132, m. Peripatetici Formas suas statuunt indivisi-</l>
    <l n="89">biles, 124, p. &amp; tamen velint nolint cogun-</l>
